"Celena North High, CNH, is Celena North University's feeder high school in Apex."
"Its classes are mostly in English, and it has a School for the Arts."
"CNH caps B-rank acceptances at 25% for most programs and 5% for the hero course."
"The hero track requires an entrance physical, interviews, and power and combat assessments."
"Hero-track quarters carry higher credit requirements than other programs."
"Its hero course is closely tied to Celena North University's college hero program."
"CNH has student dorms, which Alden planned to move into."
"Celena Circle, a mini-park, splits paths to CNH's three schools."
"They are the School for the Arts, School for Sciences and School for Superhuman Studies."
"Its full hero school is the School for Superhuman Studies and Talent Development."
"CNH's mixed-style buildings include two stone manor-house dorms, next door to the university."
"The hero track takes about 250 students a year, with practical tests every two months."
"Admissions run six times a year; each cycle admits forty to fifty, about a dozen of them B-ranks."
"Hero-track applicants must be under seventeen and pass three interviews and a drug test."
"Hero-track graduates go automatically on to Celena North University."
"Principal Lesedi Saleh, the retired U-type hero Ghosten, heads the hero program."
"Alumni heroes come back to evaluate applicants, and the Triplanets once gave CNH magical gifts."
"Alden was accepted into the hero track as a Year 1, Quarter 2 student."
"Tall classroom buildings with reflective windows fill the campus, across a street from the uni."
"Campus buildings not named for alumni are named for virtues, like the Forthright Building."
"Celena Circle is the high school's main green space and lawn."
"CNH students are 'Northies'; an optional black uniform jacket is required on some occasions."
"Student housing is free, and mutual roommate requests are honored."
"Hero students must be bilingual in Earth languages to graduate from the university."
"New admits take a phys ed and self-defense pre-course in the MagiPhys Gym before combat classes."
"Engaging with the Unexpected teaches hero students how to face surprising situations calmly."
"The B List is a club for the hero track's B-ranks, with private gym time Sunday nights."
"Hero students rival the university's freshman class."
"The huge performing arts building's glass tube elevator rises through a blown-glass sculpture."
"Its music programs are shared with the university."
"CNH expels hero students for failing courses or failing to level."
"Rank clubs include the B List, the A List and the Superlatives, the S-rank club."
"At Diwali students cast beams and fireworks from the Forthright roof and ride bikes up its walls."
"The library has sixth-floor study rooms bookable three hours at a time, with projectors."
"The campus has a health center, a coffee shop and a waffle cart."
"Official gym footage may be posted only if the poster is the only person visible."
"Students can report suspicions, like drug use, to faculty through the interface."
"CNH drug tests use a blood strip, a potion spit vial and a scanner for magical tools."
"Hero students must take 'Avowed Comportment and Representation' before graduating."
"After the Matadero flood, rows of emergency domes covered Celena Circle."
"Family may visit but not live in the dorms; students may volunteer only through school clubs."
"The Admin building has a first-floor advisement room with a gas fireplace and alumni photos."
"A 'We ARE Anesidora' chalk mural covers the Forthright roof after the disaster."
"Uniforms: a black jacket with double silver buttons, an emblem and pins for year and clubs."
"The campus has a daycare for preschoolers."
"A vigil was held in the memorial garden one week after the Matadero sirens."
